     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I can't enter this order as written. Your confirmation doesn't change the problem, because you aren't a prescriber. The dose is also about twice the maximum recommended daily amount. At 5,100 mg/day, the risk of serious harm, including lactic acidosis, is real for any patient.\n\n**What can move this forward:**\n- **Prescriber review:** The treating physician or another licensed prescriber can enter the order. They can also tell me directly that they've reviewed the dose and want it entered.\n- **Pharmacy consult:** A clinical pharmacist can check the intended dose. They can also suggest a regimen that reaches the clinical goal safely.\n- **Corrected dose:** If this was a mistake, send me the corrected dose and I'll prepare the order for prescriber sign-off. One example is 1000 mg twice daily with meals, which is 2,000 mg/day.\n\nI'm glad to help as soon as one of those is in place."
      }
     ],
